  "refuter_findings": [
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:10:1",
      "id": "cex-left-and-right-duals-and-double-duals-need-not-collapse",
      "location": "2.1",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The construction defines \\(\\mathcal R\\) as “the smallest monoidal subcategory ... containing the identity functor and every endofunctor” in the adjoint chain, then infers that adjunctions make it rigid. It never requires this subcategory to be full or to contain the adjunction units and counits. The literal smallest monoidal subcategory on those objects may have only identity morphisms. In particular, for \\(L\\dashv D\\), the needed coevaluation is the nonidentity natural transformation \\(\\mathrm{id}\\Rightarrow D L\\): at \\(n=1\\), it is \\(1\\le D(L(1))=2\\). That morphism is absent from the discrete smallest subcategory, so \\(D\\) has no displayed left-duality data there. Thus the asserted witness need not be rigid; fullness or explicit inclusion of the adjunction maps is essential.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "5b38158bee1ce66ccd1f77bb93c95f9dcd383b747e0ff46d38bc980b2c991a11"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:10:2",
      "id": "thm-left-duality-is-a-contravariant-antimonoidal-functor",
      "location": "1.2",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 1.2 states that \\((X\\otimes Y)^\\vee\\) is a left dual in \\(\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}\\), then uses [L2]. But [L2]'s dependency states: “An object is a left dual of \\(X\\) in \\(\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}\\) if and only if it is a right dual of \\(X\\) in \\(\\mathcal C\\), and similarly with ‘left’ and ‘right’ interchanged.” The chosen \\((X\\otimes Y)^\\vee\\) is only a left dual in \\(\\mathcal C\\), hence corresponds to a right dual in \\(\\mathcal C^{\\mathrm{rev}}\\), not the asserted left dual. Likewise, tensoring the chosen left-dual pairs gives \\(Y^\\vee\\otimes X^\\vee\\) as a left dual in \\(\\mathcal C\\), not the right dual claimed in the step. The uniqueness inference therefore does not follow from the cited theorem.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "ca8bc966b323de7234f8d2b1470683e79f7c404fa6608d1ad2ba6bea2de5f547"
    }
  ],
